{"level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"role":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translat